answer.worked:
For $-1\leq x\leq 1$:
$$\begin{align*}
f(x)+g(x) &= \sin^{-1}x+\cos^{-1}x \\
&= \frac{\pi}{2}
\end{align*}$$
The significance is that $\sin^{-1}x$ and $\cos^{-1}x$ are complementary angles for the same value of $x$ on the interval $-1\leq x\leq 1$. The answer is $\frac{\pi}{2}$.

