entries.description:
2022 HSC Extension 1 Band 4
Given that \cos\left(\frac{23\pi}{12}\right)=\frac{\sqrt{6}+\sqrt{2}}{4}, which of the following is the value of \cos^{-1}\left(\frac{\sqrt{6}+\sqrt{2}}{4}\right)?
A. \frac{23\pi}{12}
B. \frac{11\pi}{12}
C. \frac{\pi}{12}
D. -\frac{11\pi}{12}
